{"id":"d75bea40-0da0-4799-81e4-066def724666","object":"chat.completion","created":1785031188,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n            \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n            \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain\\n        })\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the problem: The task is AGENT-TF-01. We have a case object with \"threshold\" and \"calls\" array. Each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable. We need to compute for each call: gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens (at least one token, but prediction_tokens is given, should be integer >=1? The example shows values 2-6, so no zero). Then if parseable is true AND normalized_gain >= threshold (inclusive), then accepted. Otherwise not.\n\nThen we need to output accepted_call_ids list (order as in calls? They say \"Keep diagnostics in supplied call order\", so we should keep order of calls as in input. For diagnostics, each object with call_id, accepted (boolean), normalized_gain (number). Return accepted_call_ids list of strings (order as they appear in calls, only accepted ones). Diagnostics list in same order as calls.\n\nNote: normalized_gain should be a number, not rounded? The description says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\"? It says \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" But the output schema does not mention rounding; it says type number. We must output number. Possibly we should round? The problem says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but the schema says number. Need to interpret. Perhaps we should round to some precision? Usually in such tasks they want exact float. I'll output as computed float. But maybe round to avoid floating point issues? The sample here doesn't tell. However the output contract says type number, so we can output as float; no rounding specified. I'll compute and output the exact value. But note the problem statement: \"Stay inside this mechanism boundary... rounded per-call diagnostics.\" That suggests we should round. But to what? Could be to 8 decimal places? Or maybe truncation? The input values have many decimals, but output schema has type number. Since it's a JSON number, it can be any float. I think we should output as is. However to be safe, maybe round to a few decimals like 8? The problem says \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" but does not specify precision. Usually in these tasks, they expect the calculation to be done with floating point and output as is. I'll output as float, Python's float will be serialized as JSON number automatically.\n\nAlso note: \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" That's done.\n\nImplementation: solve(case) receives dict with threshold and calls. Return dict with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nEdge cases: threshold is 0.05 in all samples. prediction_tokens could be zero? The problem says \"at least one prediction token\", but input may have zero? Not in samples. We'll assume it's positive integer.\n\nParseable is a boolean.\n\nOutput: accepted_call_ids list of strings (call_ids where accepted true). Diagnostics list of objects in same order as calls.\n\nI'll implement solve(case) as required.\n\nNow need to output JSON with key \"implementation\" and value as Python source string. Must escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nWe'll produce the code. Use standard library only.\n\nLet's write:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case['threshold']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call['call_id']\n        parseable = call['parseable']\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\n        tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / tokens\n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain >= threshold)\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain\n        })\n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n\nThat's it.\n\nNow we need to output as JSON with key implementation. The value must be a string containing the Python source, properly escaped.\n\nWe'll produce the final JSON.\n\nMake sure no extra spaces, no markdown.\n\nWe'll output the JSON directly."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2134,"completion_tokens":1154,"total_tokens":3288,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":2048},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":927},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":2048,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":86},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}